:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99007#issuecomment-3300665432","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99007","id":3300665432,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7EvChY","user":{"login":"precup","id":709680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTY4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/709680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup","html_url":"https://github.com/precup","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-16T23:33:53Z","updated_at":"2025-09-16T23:33:53Z","body":"Ah, I see. It looks like the sidebar got collapsed at some point. If you click on the arrow circled below, it'll expand out a panel like my terrible drawing:\n\n<img width=\"1173\" height=\"867\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6ebd398c-f304-44ae-a8dd-ff3000f49d17\" />\n\nThat panel is the control menu for the script editor. The bar at the top is for scenes, not scripts, so not adding anything there is correct.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3300665432/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3300721991","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99007#issuecomment-3300721991","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99007","id":3300721991,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7EvQVH","user":{"login":"cedarbob","id":30355407,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzU1NDA3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30355407?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedarbob","html_url":"https://github.com/cedarbob","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedarbob/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedarbob/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedarbob/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedarbob/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedarbob/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedarbob/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedarbob/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedarbob/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedarbob/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-17T00:04:46Z","updated_at":"2025-09-17T00:04:46Z","body":"I still think there is an issue here, because in Script mode versus 2D mode, a script is displayed in the window instead of a graphical scene.  So the tab label of the window in Script mode should be the name of the script being displayed and not the name of a scene (which may be completely unrelated to the script).","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3300721991/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3300739998","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99007#issuecomment-3300739998","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99007","id":3300739998,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7EvUue","user":{"login":"precup","id":709680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTY4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/709680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup","html_url":"https://github.com/precup","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-17T00:14:02Z","updated_at":"2025-09-17T00:14:02Z","body":"> I still think there is an issue here, because in Script mode versus 2D mode, a script is displayed in the window instead of a graphical scene. So the tab label of the window in Script mode should be the name of the script being displayed and not the name of a scene (which may be completely unrelated to the script).\n\nThe scene is actually still running in the background. If you have a tool script, for instance, it will still continue executing while in Script mode. The current scene is also still important for things like hitting the Run Current Scene button, for instance. When you're working on a scene, you might switch between 2D, 3D, and Script repeatedly but still be working on the same scene, or you may wish to switch scenes while staying in Script mode.\n\nNote also that *none* of the modes available at the top change the scene or scene tab bar at all. Switching between them doesn't impact what the current scene is, so leaving it displayed and changeable makes sense. It's still relevant and useful in Script mode.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3300739998/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3303396654","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99007#issuecomment-3303396654","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99007","id":3303396654,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7E5dUu","user":{"login":"cedarbob","id":30355407,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzU1NDA3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30355407?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedarbob","html_url":"https://github.com/cedarbob","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedarbob/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedarbob/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedarbob/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedarbob/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedarbob/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedarbob/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedarbob/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedarbob/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedarbob/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-17T14:53:53Z","updated_at":"2025-09-17T14:53:53Z","body":"The current scene is already identified in the window title bar.  So it is redundant to put it in the tab label.  Using the tab label to identify what you are looking at on the tab page makes more sense to me from a usability standpoint. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3303396654/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3303451553","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99007#issuecomment-3303451553","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99007","id":3303451553,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7E5quh","user":{"login":"precup","id":709680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTY4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/709680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup","html_url":"https://github.com/precup","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-17T15:07:56Z","updated_at":"2025-09-17T15:07:56Z","body":"The tab bar doesn't just show you the current tab, it allows you to change it. Needing to switch out of Script mode any time you wanted to change scenes is an extra step that isn't necessary and would hurt usability. The scene switcher people are used to disappearing but only in certain cases seems potentially confusing, as well.\n\nHaving two separate tab selectors for two functionally distinct sets of open files seems correct to me. I don't see why we would remove one when both are useful. If you think the placement or positioning should change, I think that's arguable, but not displaying both while in Script mode is something I'm strongly opposed to.\n\nAs an additional example, I'll also note that the Scene Tree and Inspector are still available for the current scene while in Script mode. What if you want to see the Scene Tree from a different scene? The option to switch should be available in all modes.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3303451553/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]